{
  "analysis": "I see the R_InitTextures allocations. The 25MB allocation likely comes from `temp3` which is computed as `((temp2-temp1+63)/64) + ((numtextures+63)/64)` and then `Z_Malloc(temp3, ...)` for texturecolumnlump/ofs data. I need to see the full computation and check if numtextures is reasonable. The issue could be an interpreter bug in arithmetic or load operations. I should add tracing to Z_Malloc to see the exact sequence of allocations.",
  "plan": "Inspect the full R_InitTextures function around temp3 computation, find the Z_Malloc symbol address, and add tracing to the VM to log Z_Malloc calls with size and return address. This will identify which allocation is 25MB.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '470,580p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/r_data.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "readelf -s /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -E \"Z_Malloc\" | head -5\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
